{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 459 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "20b612d12708a6b54f1e12baf8fd11b2305576a8708c7af907ac5081a1d601e5" :edb/db-before-t 458 :edb/db-after-t 459 :edb/tx-data [[13194139533771 50 #inst "2026-10-04T21:20:25.709Z" 13194139533771 true] [17592186096662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250097 13194139533771 true] [17592186096662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250104 13194139533771 true] [17592186096662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250111 13194139533771 true] [17592186096662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250118 13194139533771 true] [17592186096662 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250125 13194139533771 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250083 13194139533771 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250132 13194139533771 true] [17592186096763 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250135 13194139533771 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250069 13194139533771 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250076 13194139533771 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250090 13194139533771 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250129 13194139533771 true] [17592186096764 1020 #edb/ref 17592186250138 13194139533771 true] [17592186096946 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533771 true] [17592186096946 1145 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=3{x}^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)=(3x+5)^{2}.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=6x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=6(3x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(6x){(3x+5)}^{2}-(3{x}^{2})\\cdot 6(3x+5)}{{((3x+5)^{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(3x+5-3x)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{6x(3x+5)(5)}{{(3x+5)}^{4}} \\\\  & =\\frac{30x}{{(3x+5)}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186097119 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533771 true] [17592186097119 1145 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)$ and the denominator $v(x)=4x.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=4.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(7{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2))(4x)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)(4)}{(4x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{16{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{⧸}4(7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2))}{\\text{⧸}4(4{x}^{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{7x{sec}^{2}⁡(7x-2)-\\operatorname{tan}⁡(7x-2)}{4{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250070 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1089 "q-10009" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1100 "Find the slope of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x$ at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1113 #uuid "af401821-15de-511b-ae7d-83263ee65d61" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250069 1145 "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u$ and $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x)(\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x)+(\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x)(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡3x-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡3x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=\\pi /2} & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2})\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250071 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250072 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250073 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250074 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250075 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1041 "selection" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250074 13194139533771 true] [17592186250070 1110 #uuid "6fd66f9f-c00b-54af-af6e-42d63823f63d" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250071 1034 "3" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250071 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250071 1111 #uuid "e379f4ed-96fc-54e8-8343-e7cc7dbd548b" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250072 1034 "2" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250072 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250072 1111 #uuid "2f09a3ed-5703-5d97-89c0-061a8ca7796a" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250073 1034 "1" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250073 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250073 1111 #uuid "d67420c2-d9f9-5af0-8fa1-6c7483fbc14a" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250074 1034 "0" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250074 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250074 1111 #uuid "e8067465-e26d-5981-81be-8eb81be4480d" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250075 1034 "-1" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250075 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250075 1111 #uuid "f3f0ffea-2d18-5020-a1b2-92d74de3da0a" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250077 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1089 "q-11824" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1100 "Given that $y=(x+1){e}^{9x},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1113 #uuid "ac4f2143-0b5a-5a4d-94fb-d6c2015bc5dd" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250076 1145 "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=x+1$ and $v(x)={e}^{9x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=1,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=9{e}^{9x}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(1)({e}^{9x})+(x+1)(9{e}^{9x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{9x}+9(x+1){e}^{9x} \\\\  & =(1+9(x+1)){e}^{9x} \\\\  & =(9x+10){e}^{9x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250078 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250079 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250080 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250081 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250082 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1041 "selection" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250079 13194139533771 true] [17592186250077 1110 #uuid "b81c9e8f-3785-5c2e-a976-836a987cad2d" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250078 1034 "9x{e}^{9x}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250078 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250078 1111 #uuid "ab3aa463-cd3f-5a68-8b33-e28f2c51b2a8" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250079 1034 "(9x+10){e}^{9x}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250079 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250079 1111 #uuid "39574bcf-9d44-56f9-89f4-8cb38b5f0839" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250080 1034 "(9x+1){e}^{9x}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250080 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250080 1111 #uuid "30de3564-36c3-5b89-a7d1-0ac882a7a75e" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250081 1034 "(x+1){e}^{9x}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250081 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250081 1111 #uuid "f8cc61d7-1d4e-550e-abaf-a727fc21ef7a" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250082 1034 "9(x+1){e}^{9x}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250082 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250082 1111 #uuid "daf469be-b289-52dd-8823-1062d5390f95" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250084 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1089 "q-11978" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1100 "Given that $y=\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{x}^{2}+1},$ find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1113 #uuid "92523772-6de5-5832-955f-4e96488833e4" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250083 1145 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=(x+1)^{2}$ and the denominator $v(x)={x}^{2}+1.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2(x+1),\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(2(x+1))({x}^{2}+1)-((x+1)^{2})(2x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)({x}^{2}+1)-2x(x+1)^{2}}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)(({x}^{2}+1)-x(x+1))}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)({x}^{2}+1-{x}^{2}-x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(x+1)(1-x)}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(1-{x}^{2})}{({x}^{2}+1)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250085 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250086 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250087 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250088 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250089 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1041 "selection" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250086 13194139533771 true] [17592186250084 1110 #uuid "a69f7ba6-4320-560f-9024-6f57f32bc283" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250085 1034 "\\frac{(1-2{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250085 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250085 1111 #uuid "9edca068-3380-5f7b-8546-48890d080555" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250086 1034 "\\frac{2(1-{x}^{2})}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250086 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250086 1111 #uuid "350a83e0-7923-5b08-9392-87ad87b493ef" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250087 1034 "\\frac{2(x+1)}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250087 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250087 1111 #uuid "0d475a46-ac9e-5a93-a5f8-a773369ddfa7" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250088 1034 "\\frac{2(1-x)}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250088 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250088 1111 #uuid "447e4b73-1241-5aa4-b059-4f8b11f3010d" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250089 1034 "\\frac{(1-x)^{2}}{{({x}^{2}+1)}^{2}}" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250089 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250089 1111 #uuid "80b1e053-447b-51ae-ad6d-1678ce0ad780" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1017 #edb/ref 17592186250091 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1089 "q-2392" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1100 "Calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y={a}^{3x}\\operatorname{tan}⁡x.$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1113 #uuid "3cc0b95c-1856-5de2-836b-234ed6403eea" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250090 1145 "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)=\\operatorname{tan}⁡x$ and $v(x)={a}^{3x}.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)={sec}^{2}⁡x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{a}^{3x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡a.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =({sec}^{2}⁡x)({a}^{3x})+(\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)(3{a}^{3x}\\operatorname{ln}⁡a) \\\\  & ={a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡a\\operatorname{tan}⁡x).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250092 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250093 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250094 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250095 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1000 #edb/ref 17592186250096 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1041 "selection" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1104 #edb/ref 17592186250096 13194139533771 true] [17592186250091 1110 #uuid "6bb343fc-e533-5bb4-8af7-1e974f8437a0" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250092 1034 "{a}^{3x}{sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250092 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250092 1111 #uuid "0e72bb9e-bf50-5f05-8fea-6643e8e5c873" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250093 1034 "3{a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+\\operatorname{ln}⁡a\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250093 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533771 true] [17592186250093 1111 #uuid "4ca4322b-0aa8-589a-b696-325d8ce56f43" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250094 1034 "{a}^{3x}({sec}^{2}⁡x+3\\operatorname{tan}⁡x)" 13194139533771 true] [17592186250094 1103 #e